[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all! I wanted to share a project I've recently completed called \"ship your interpreter\"!</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/</a></p>\n<p>Formal Semantics are a necessary precursor to enable program verification. Unfortunately most programming languages do not have any semantics.</p>\n<p>One might be tempted to use LLMs to generate these semantics, but as semantics form part of your trusted spec, and semantics for real world languages tend to be very complex, these artefacts are large and hard to trust.</p>\n<p>Can we get LLMs to build program semantics that can be trusted?</p>\n<p>Answer? Yes! Ship your interpreter! That is you can compile your programming language interpreter to RISCV (which has a formal model in Lean), and then validate the LLM generated semantics by proving that the interpreter refines the big step semantics:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"2520x1748\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/yvmILHW-n6BXtLb-2rh5xTUP/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/yvmILHW-n6BXtLb-2rh5xTUP/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>Ship your interpreters repository contains an MVP for this approach, consisting of an interpreter for a small WHILE language written in C (lexer, parser and a tree-walking evaluator with closures, strings and runtime errors), compiled to a bare-metal RV64 ELF.</p>\n<p>Vsa/While/Semantics.lean contains the (LLM-generated) big-step semantics:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EvalE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">St</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Addr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">St</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">St</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Addr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">EvalE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">St</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Addr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">EvalE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Which overall, is quite readable.</p>\n<p>The headline theorem is in VsaIris/Interp/EndToEnd.lean:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endToEnd_refinement</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Loaded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">interpRunLayout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fillZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Halts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Diverges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>That is, for any program AST p and any RISC-V machine configuration c with p loaded in memory, the Sail model halts printing out with exit code 0 exactly when the big-step semantics says p outputs out. And if the machine diverges, the semantics has no derivation.</p>\n<p>This project also uses the recently released iris-lean project! The project was really struggling without it, and after porting, it finished in a few days Huge thanks to the iris-lean folks!</p>\n<p>The north star of this approach would be an LLM generated semantics for CPython. I believe this is entirely feasible with the capabilities of modern agents. You just need to dump a ton of compute into it.</p>\n<p>Discussion thread: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Discussion.20for.20Ship.20Your.20Interpreters/with/627253909\">#general &gt; Discussion for Ship Your Interpreters</a></p>",
        "id": 627249674,
        "sender_full_name": "Kiran",
        "timestamp": 1790533894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Once you have this kind of verified semantics, you can build a number of additional end-to-end <em>verified</em> tools by bootstrapping on top of this refinement theorem:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Verified type system</em>: You can prove progress and preservation against the big-step semantics, and type safety carries down to the RISCV assembly:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type_soundness</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WellTyped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ExecSeqErrN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initSt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStepDiverges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Well-typed programs only ever fail with division by zero, a failed assert, or the call-depth cap. <br>\nPR: <a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/1\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/1</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Program logics for verification</em>: You can use the big step semantics to produce a program logic for verifying programs in the language:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">adequacy_machine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initOwn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wpSeq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PostOut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Loaded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">interpRunLayout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fillZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Halts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Diverges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>PR: <a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/2\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/2</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Verified abstract interpretation/static analyses</em>: You can build static analyses for the language and prove that they are sound (no false alarms):</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">no_error_of_no_alarms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">alarms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cfg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStepErr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>PR: <a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/3\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/3</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Verified AOT Compiler</em>: Once you have the formal semantics, you can effectively drop the binary, and treat the LLM generated semantics as the source of truth, and construct your own compiler (verified) for the language:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">compile_correct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Program</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hsup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Supported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Config</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">compileBytes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">c.σ.mem</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0x80004800</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">compileBytes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Halts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Diverges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BigStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>PR: <a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/4\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-interpreter/pull/4</a></p>\n<p>Just imagine the same being done for Python! What a time to be alive!</p>",
        "id": 627250295,
        "sender_full_name": "Kiran",
        "timestamp": 1790534294
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Really cool! Is there a discussion thread on Zulip for follow-up questions? Or a different preferred forum?</p>",
        "id": 627253515,
        "sender_full_name": "Li Xuanji",
        "timestamp": 1790536436
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh yep let me make a thread for it: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Discussion.20for.20Ship.20Your.20Interpreters/with/627253909\">#general &gt; Discussion for Ship Your Interpreters</a></p>",
        "id": 627253955,
        "sender_full_name": "Kiran",
        "timestamp": 1790536707
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Follow-up: I've now written up a blog post with more details about this!</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.basis.ai/blog/ship-your-interpreters/\">https://www.basis.ai/blog/ship-your-interpreters/</a></p>\n<p>The post is written for a broader audience than this thread, but covers a few additional things not in the original announcement post:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the specific bugs in the semantics the proof helped the agent to find.</li>\n<li>the reason why <code>malloc</code> became a blocker before the iris-lean port: in particular, for whatever reason the agents were unable to figure out SL themselves even when asked, and kept on writing specifications with fixed sets of locations that could be modified (this is part of the answer to <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"989743\">@Jack McCarthy</span>'s questions in the discussion thread)</li>\n<li>the performance numbers for the verified compiler from WHILE to RISC-V,  coming out to 2.7–8.2× faster than the original interpreter</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Since then I have also been in the background running a few agents to try tackling Lua 5.4 and OCaml's bytecode interpreter (<a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-lua\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-lua</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-ocaml\">https://github.com/BasisResearch/ship-your-ocaml</a>)</p>\n<p>Come round to NYC Lean next week by when I will have scrounged up some kind of presentation of these results!</p>",
        "id": 632798162,
        "sender_full_name": "Kiran",
        "timestamp": 1792335041
    }
]